          "title": "You'll want to know: मथ्नाति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मथ्नाति — mathnāti — \"churns\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माता दधि मथ्नाति। mātā dadhi mathnāti. Mother churns the curd."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (she …): सा दधि मथितवती, sā dadhi mathitavatī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मथ्नाति (mathnāti) comes from the root √math (also manth), \"to stir, to churn\", whose present is mathnāti; its past participle is mathita (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
